Major changes compared with the original (2026, Esoren):
  - Rewritten for the Paper/Purpur 26.2 API and Java 25; the original 2014
    code was used as a reference only.
  - Generation runs in a BlockPopulator on the LimitedRegion; no asynchronous
    world access and no fixed 128-block world height.
  - Vein passes are defined in config.yml (material, host rock, attempts,
    size, Y range, distribution, biomes, spawn chance, air-exposure discard);
    Y values scale to each world's real height.
  - The generator's own overworld and Nether ores are removed first; removed
    blocks are filled with the dominant neighbouring block.
  - Deepslate ore variants, deep obsidian/magma/lava bodies.
  - One-time retrofit of existing chunks, manual regeneration commands and a
    restart-safe "regenerate all" over every chunk on disk.
  - English and German messages.
